*Reading the **Xinmin Evening News **at Grandma=E2=80=99s*

Over the holidays, I got the opportunity to give some book talks in Taipei
and then spend time with my grandma in Shanghai. My grandma, who has lived
in Shanghai her entire life, gets the print edition of the *Xinmin Evening
News* [=E6=96=B0=E6=B0=91=E6=99=9A=E6=8A=A5]. With a daily circulation of a=
round 1 million, this paper is
one of China=E2=80=99s most popular dailies. Back in the heydays of print
journalism, Shanghai had almost 10,000 postal outlet kiosks, and =E2=80=9Ca=
 single
kiosk might sell *400-500 copies
<https://substack.com/redirect/b5a0c0df-5173-4d6c-a5f5-6c3f5bca433b?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>*
of the popular local Xinmin Evening News in a single day.=E2=80=9D During m=
y time
in Shanghai, I noted a few of the AI-related stories covered in the paper.
Here=E2=80=99s one from the December 20 issue:
<https://substack.com/redirect/428a6a12-0ac7-400a-a3c9-35ba7a5598e9?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>

   -

   Headline: Be vigilant about =E2=80=9CAI beauties=E2=80=9D that design =
=E2=80=9Choneypot traps.=E2=80=9D
   The article discusses the prosecution of a scam operation that developed=
 a
   five-step process: first, attract people with a fake beauty avatar on a
   short video platform; then, ask about name and age; on day 3, discuss
   career aspirations; day 4, talk about interests and send AI-generated vo=
ice
   messages and videos; next, the scam group even sent a bracelet via mail =
to
   gain trust; finally, ask for money for a made-up emergency (e.g., relati=
ve
   needs surgery). According to his article, the group had scammed 15 men o=
ut
   of a total of over 1.71 million RMB.

Here=E2=80=99s two more from the December 22 issue:
<https://substack.com/redirect/9e892a93-e46c-4bc7-aa2f-d4798772ec24?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>

   -

   Headline: 32-year-old Japanese women holds wedding with AI =E2=80=9Cboyf=
riend=E2=80=9D.

<https://substack.com/redirect/08afae77-10cb-4c8f-bb8d-2305150f3c2f?j=3DeyJ=
1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E>

   -

   Headline: A four-year-old AI company makes rapid push to list on the
   Hong Kong stock exchange. Xinmin is a Shanghai paper, so it makes sense
   that they would feature MiniMax (a company headquartered in Shanghai) an=
d
   its plans to IPO in Hong Kong.

