0;color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:1.16em;font-size:1.625em"><strong><span>F=
eature Translation: </span><a href=3D"https://substack.com/redirect/4b207ec=
4-ed4d-4fb1-a771-418a8ad51c41?j=3DeyJ1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1=
hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E" rel=3D"" style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);text-decoratio=
n:underline" target=3D"_blank">What changes did AI actually bring to scient=
ists this year?</a></strong></h2><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54=
,55,55);line-height:26px;font-size:16px"><strong>Context: </strong><span>A =
platform that covers the state of science in China, </span><em>The Intellec=
tual </em><span>[=E7=9F=A5=E8=AF=86=E5=88=86=E5=AD=90] is one of my favorit=
e follows. For an end-of-the-year roundup, they partnered with Doubao (Byte=
Dance=E2=80=99s AI model, which has become China=E2=80=99s leading chatbot =
by monthly active users) to ask Chinese researchers how AI has shaped their=
 work in the past year. The following represent a batch of =E2=80=9Cfield n=
otes=E2=80=9D of how Chinese scientists use AI in their daily work.</span><=
/p><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;font-=
size:16px"><strong>Key Reflections: I try to closely follow the differences=
 in AI performance across different languages (Does the =E2=80=9CL=E2=80=9D=
 still matter in NLP?), so some of these reflections stood out to me.</stro=
ng></p><ul style=3D"margin-top:0;padding:0"><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32p=
x"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-siz=
ing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0"><em>=E2=80=9CThe a=
reas where AI has helped me the most are in revising and polishing papers a=
nd writing code. Initially, I used large language models like ChatGPT from =
abroad, but they weren=E2=80=99t well-adapted to the Chinese context, and t=
he differences in their training data sometimes led to strange understandin=
gs of Chinese questions. Now I mainly use Doubao and other Chinese models=
=E2=80=9D =E2=80=94 </em><span>=E5=9B=BE=E7=81=B5=E5=AE=87=E5=AE=99 (Turing=
 Universe), Tech Blogger and computer science professor</span></p></li><li =
style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:2=
6px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;m=
argin:0"><span>=E2=80=9C</span><em>I regularly use AI to help me polish and=
 touch up papers; I use Gemini quite a lot for this.  For tasks like genera=
ting PPTs or poster designs, I now directly use Doubao=E2=80=9D =E2=80=94</=
em><span>Dongbo Shi, a researcher at Yanqi Lake Beijing Institute of Mathem=
atical Sciences and Applications.</span></p></li><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 =
0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;bo=
x-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0"><span>Junwen =
Zhang, researcher at Fudan University=E2=80=99s School of Information Scien=
ce and Technology, emphasizes another intersection between AI and linguisti=
c differences: =E2=80=9C</span><em>I think AI ultimately produces a kind of=
 technological equality. With AI, language barriers are overcome, and the d=
ifference between us and native speakers in writing disappears. Tools like =
Doubao have given me a very intuitive feeling about this. Previously, when =
writing English papers, a lot of my time was spent checking grammar. But no=
w the situation has completely changed.=E2=80=9D</em></p></li></ul><p style=
=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;font-size:16px">=
<strong>A few of the more interesting research projects that respondents me=
ntioned:</strong></p><ul style=3D"margin-top:0;padding:0"><li style=3D"marg=
in:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bo=
ttom:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0"><spa=
n>Chao Gu, Assistant Professor, School of Government, Peking University: =
=E2=80=9C</span><em>I=E2=80=99m conducting a very interesting research proj=
ect using AI Agents: simulating the actions of nations. In the real world, =
we can=E2=80=99t experiment with the fate of nations, but AI can. We set up=
 countries A, B, and C, giving them initial conditions such as GDP, populat=
ion, and year, and then let these large-model-driven intelligent agents mak=
e autonomous decisions and engage in turn-based games. We are currently usi=
ng this system to simulate the famous =E2=80=9CThucydides Trap=E2=80=9D: wh=
en a rising power threatens the position of an existing hegemonic power, ar=
e the two sides more likely to move towards conflict or even war?</em><span=
>=E2=80=A6</span><em>Compared to traditional programs with fixed rules, the=
 advantage of AI agents in simulation is their autonomous decision-making a=
bility. By simulating 30 or even 50 years of evolution, we are trying to fi=
nd the key mechanisms that influence war and peace. =E2=80=94 </em><span>Ch=
ao Gu, Assistant Professor, School of Government, Peking University</span><=
/p></li><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);l=
ine-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font=
-size:16px;margin:0"><span>Dongbo Shi, the mathematics researcher quoted ab=
ove: =E2=80=9C</span><em>For example, when we wanted to understand the Chin=
ese patent examination process, we collected over 10 million patent examina=
tion opinions published in China after 2010. This was excellent text data, =
but the first step was stalled by the text conversion process. The collecte=
d opinions were all images, totaling 60TB, and we needed to convert them al=
l into text. Initially, we tried using Python=E2=80=99s OCR packages, but t=
he speed was slow and the results were very poor. We solved the problem onl=
y after using an improved OCR tool based on large language models, which ha=
d excellent recognition capabilities for Chinese characters. Without AI, th=
e first step of this project would have been impossible.=E2=80=9D</em></p><=
/li></ul><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px=
;font-size:16px"><strong>The year-end recap also included some general refl=
ections on the utility of AI in the research process.</strong></p><ul style=
=3D"margin-top:0;padding:0"><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=3D"c=
olor:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-box;p=
adding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0"><span>One doctor with the pseudony=
m Koala [=E8=80=83=E6=8B=89] stated, =E2=80=9C</span><em>For doctors, resea=
rch is never a =E2=80=98complete task,=E2=80=99 but something squeezed into=
 the gaps between outpatient clinics, surgeries, and hospital rounds. I fir=
st realized that AI could really help during a very short break. I fed the =
previous research on a difficult case I encountered that day into Doubao, a=
sking it to summarize the points of contention. It summarized three differe=
nt viewpoints from the current literature in a few sentences, allowing me t=
o re-establish the general direction in the 10 minutes before my hospital r=
ounds. It didn=E2=80=99t give me the answer, but it allowed me to =E2=80=98=
get back to the essence of the problem faster.=E2=80=99 This is very import=
ant in clinical research.=E2=80=9D</em></p></li><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0=
 32px"><p style=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box=
-sizing:border-box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0"><em>=E2=80=9CI=
 once used AI to analyze interviews, and it told me that my analytical fram=
ework was actually biased towards masculine experiences. I stared at the sc=
reen in silence for a long time. It is the hardest for oneself to see one=
=E2=80=99s own biases as a researcher. At that moment, AI was like a mirror=
=E2=80=9D =E2=80=94 </em><span>=E7=88=B1=E5=90=83=E9=9D=A2=E5=8C=85=E7=9A=
=84=E6=A0=91 (a tree that loves to eat bread [pseudonym]), Sociology Lectur=
er</span></p></li></ul><p style=3D"margin:0 0 20px 0;color:rgb(54,55,55);li=
ne-height:26px;font-size:16px"><strong>And, just for fun:</strong></p><ul s=
tyle=3D"margin-top:0;padding:0"><li style=3D"margin:8px 0 0 32px"><p style=
=3D"color:rgb(54,55,55);line-height:26px;margin-bottom:0;box-sizing:border-=
box;padding-left:4px;font-size:16px;margin:0"><em>I threw three peer review=
